abstract: >-
  Mining and Metallurgy Heritage Ontology (MMHO, 矿冶遗存本体) is a
  domain ontology for knowledge organization of pre-Qin and Han
  mining and metallurgy heritage sites. MMHO adopts OWL 2 DL encoding
  and aligns with CIDOC CRM v7.1.3, the international reference
  ontology for cultural heritage information. The ontology organizes
  the domain knowledge through a three-layer structure (site-feature-
  artifact), covering the complete technological chain from ore
  extraction through smelting and casting to product disposal. v1.6.0
  contains 97 classes, 41 object properties, 230 instances, and 1,869
  axioms with DL expressivity SOIFI.
